# Shell scripts must keep LF, even on a Windows checkout. With core.autocrlf=true git writes them
# out with CRLF, and `docker build` copies the working-tree file verbatim - the container then
# cannot exec `#!/bin/sh\r` and fails with a bare "not found". That silently broke the web image's
# runtime-config entrypoint, the script that writes config.js at container start.
*.sh text eol=lf
